Subject: [qnx-porter 0001] endian-netbyte
Source: deterministic rule
Reason: `be32toh` comes from glibc's <endian.h>, which QNX 8.0 does not have. QNX has the same names as BSD macros in <net/netbyte.h>; a small header (-included in every compile) includes it and defines any name strict POSIX flags hid, from QNX's __NET_BE*/__NET_LE* helpers.
Error: /home/chirag/qnx800/host/linux/x86_64/usr/bin/aarch64-unknown-nto-qnx8.0.0-ld: ../src/libpaho-mqtt3c.so.1.3.16: undefined reference to `be32toh'
